  "info": {
    "title": "AI Data Quality Platform Review API",
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/review-cases": {
      "get": {
        "description": "One page of the queue, optionally filtered by status.\n\n``status`` is the ``ReviewStatus`` enum, so FastAPI matches it exactly:\n``PENDING`` is accepted and ``pending`` is a 422. Coercing case would mean\nthis layer deciding what a status token means, and there is already exactly\none answer to that in ``human_review.models``.\n\nFiltering is the repository's job and slicing is this route's. ``total``\ncounts the filtered set before the slice, so an offset past the end returns\nan empty page that still says how many cases matched.",
        "operationId": "list_review_cases_api_v1_review_cases_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Exact review status.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "status",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReviewStatus"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Exact review status.",
              "title": "Status"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 50,
              "maximum": 200,
              "minimum": 1,
              "title": "Limit",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "offset",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 0,
              "minimum": 0,
              "title": "Offset",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReviewCaseListResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List review cases",
        "tags": [
          "review-cases"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/review-cases/{review_case_id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Full detail for one case, including the version a resolution must echo.\n\n``get_case`` raises ``ReviewCaseNotFoundError`` for an unknown id, which the\nregistered handler turns into a 404 with a static message.",
        "operationId": "get_review_case_api_v1_review_cases__review_case_id__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "review_case_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
              "maxLength": 128,
              "minLength": 1,
              "title": "Review Case Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReviewCaseDetail"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get one review case",
        "tags": [
          "review-cases"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/review-cases/{review_case_id}/events": {
      "get": {
        "description": "The append-only history, oldest first, in the repository's own order.\n\n``get_case`` runs first only to produce the 404: ``list_events`` answers an\nunknown case and an eventless case identically.",
        "operationId": "list_case_events_api_v1_review_cases__review_case_id__events_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "review_case_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
              "maxLength": 128,
              "minLength": 1,
              "title": "Review Case Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReviewEventRead"
                  },
                  "title": "Response List Case Events Api V1 Review Cases  Review Case Id  Events Get",
                  "type": "array"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List a case's history",
        "tags": [
          "review-cases"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/review-cases/{review_case_id}/resolve": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Apply one human decision, through the Sprint 08 authority and nothing else.\n\nThis route decides nothing. It validates three transport fields, hands them\nto ``ReviewQueueService.resolve_case``, and projects what came back. Every\ninput the authority actually reads -- the AUTO_MATCH graph, the entity\nrecords, the entity-resolution config and its thresholds, the queue's\ncurrent state -- is loaded from storage by the service. None of it can be\nsupplied, influenced, or narrowed from here, and the request model has no\nfield through which a client could try.\n\nThat matters because Sprint 08 authorization is not a property of the\nreviewed pair. It projects a connected component across every AUTO_MATCH\nedge and every recorded human decision, so a MATCH that is safe in isolation\ncan be unsafe in context. A route that fetched one case and reasoned about\nit would silently weaken the check; this one cannot, because it never sees\nthe material.\n\nNo write happens before the domain approves. The service calls\n``ReviewWorkflow.resolve_case`` first and opens the storage transaction only\nwith what the workflow returned, so a refusal leaves no version bump, no\ntimestamp change and no history row. The refusals arrive here as Sprint 08\nand Sprint 10 exceptions, each mapped to its own status and static message\nin ``review_api.errors``.\n\n``200``, not ``201``: the case already existed and was transitioned. Nothing\nwas created at a new location.\n\n``expected_version`` is mandatory and is never defaulted to the stored\nvalue. Optimistic concurrency is the contract -- a reviewer decides against\nthe version they were shown, and one who lost the race is told so rather\nthan having their decision applied to a queue state they never saw.",
        "operationId": "resolve_review_case_api_v1_review_cases__review_case_id__resolve_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "review_case_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Stable Sprint 08 review case identifier.",
              "maxLength": 128,
              "minLength": 1,
              "title": "Review Case Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
